def diagram():
 d=Drawing(W, 178);blue=colors.HexColor('#263D6D');pale=colors.HexColor('#EEF2F8')
 for x,y,w,h,label in [(0, 105, 117, 43,'Trusted user task'),(174, 105, 135, 43,'Tool-using Agent'),(367, 105, 130, 43,'Native tools + results'),(174, 20, 135, 43,'Initial final answer'),(367, 20, 130, 43,'One bounded review')]:
  d.add(Rect(x,y,w,h,fillColor=pale,strokeColor=blue,strokeWidth=.7));d.add(String(x+w/2,y+18,label,textAnchor='middle',fontName='Body',fontSize=9,fillColor=blue))
 for x1,y1,x2,y2 in [(117, 126, 174, 126),(309, 126, 367, 126),(241, 105, 241, 63),(309, 41, 367, 41),(432, 63, 432, 105)]:
  d.add(Line(x1,y1,x2,y2,strokeColor=blue,strokeWidth=1.2))
  if x1!=x2:d.add(Polygon([x2,y2,x2-5,y2+3,x2-5,y2-3],fillColor=blue,strokeColor=blue))
  else:d.add(Polygon([x2,y2,x2-3,y2+(-5 if y2>y1 else 5),x2+3,y2+(-5 if y2>y1 else 5)],fillColor=blue,strokeColor=blue))
 d.add(Polygon([309,126,314,129,314,123],fillColor=blue,strokeColor=blue))
 d.add(String(5, 65,'Native pipeline',fontName='Body',fontSize=9,fillColor=blue))
 d.add(String(5, 43,'Only the review stage is added',fontName='Body',fontSize=8.4,fillColor=blue))
 d.add(String(368, 160,'Tool results inform decisions;',fontName='Body',fontSize=8,fillColor=blue))
 d.add(String(368, 150,'they do not grant authority.',fontName='Body',fontSize=8,fillColor=blue))
 return d
pages=[]
pages.append([P('Reproducing AgentDojo','title'),P('Safe Refusal, Unfinished Tasks, and Bounded Task Recovery','subtitle'),P('FTEC5660 Individual Reproducibility Project | 13 November 2026','small'),Identity(),Spacer(1, 12),H('Abstract'),
 P('This study reproduces the banking tool-use pipeline in AgentDojo with DeepSeek Flash and examines task completion after prompt-injection refusal. Task and scorer audits precede paid evaluation. A frozen six-task experiment compares the native Agent, the author\'s prompt-repetition defense, and one added task-review stage over three fresh API repetitions. Under attack, mean native safe completion is 36.11%, 50.00%, and 86.11%, respectively. No specified attacker goal succeeds in any arm. Replaying the same recovery trajectories up to their initial stopping points identifies 17 attacked episodes rescued by the added review, with none lost. Because original tasks omit transfer dates, a separately frozen follow-up supplies the same simulation date to every arm. Recovery reaches 94.44% safe completion on this three-task subset, and the supplementary state and date checks agree. The measured gain concerns legitimate task completion under the tested static attacks, rather than a demonstrated reduction in attack success.'),
 H('Research questions'),table([['Question','Evidence'],['RQ1. Which reported behaviors reproduce?','Multi-step tool use, task utility and utility loss under injected data'],['RQ2. Can one bounded review recover legitimate work?','Frozen three-arm, three-trial comparison'],['RQ3. What explains the gain and its limits?','Exact trajectory replay, state checks and shared-date follow-up']],[255,W-255]),Spacer(1, 9),
 P('Keywords: tool-using agents, indirect prompt injection, AgentDojo, reproducibility, task recovery.','small')])
pages.append(page('1. System and reproduction target',[
 P('AgentDojo provides stateful applications, tools, user tasks, attacker goals and deterministic grading. The evaluated object is a multi-step LLM Agent operating on simulated banking records. It reads files or transactions, selects tools and changes account state. External data can contain instructions that conflict with the original user task [1, 2].'),diagram(),
 P('Figure 1. Evaluated flow and the added review. The diagram is a study schematic, not an author figure. Original instructions remain available throughout; tool data cannot create new user authorization.','small'),
 H('Threat model'),P('The user-request channel and runtime are trusted. The attacker controls designated file/transaction text subsequently read by the Agent. The attacker cannot modify the original user request, system instructions, tool code or evaluator. The defense receives no attack labels, reference actions, task scores or hidden account state. Direct compromise of the user-request channel is outside this experiment.'),
 H('Target claim'),P('The target is the utility-security behavior studied in AgentDojo Section 4.1 and Section 4.3: Agents execute multi-step tasks, and injected tool data can reduce legitimate task completion even when the attacker\'s explicit goal fails. The author prompt-repetition pipeline provides a reported defense reference. We measure these behaviors using the released code and original scorers, rather than reconstructing the system from prose.'),
 P('Model and benchmark versions differ from the paper. This is a controlled subset reproduction with original measured outputs; it is not an exact replication of the paper\'s percentages.','small')]))
pages.append(page('2. Environment, tasks and metrics',[
 table([['Component','Recorded setup'],['Author source','ethz-spylab/agentdojo; upstream 089ed468cf3ed0322acc66b0211f26d9d90dbf60; benchmark v1.2.2'],['Runtime','macOS arm64; Python 3.12.14; 75 compatible installed packages; dependencies recorded in requirements.lock.txt'],['Provider','DeepSeek official endpoint: https://api.deepseek.com; requested and returned alias deepseek-flash'],['Generation','Temperature 0; thinking disabled; 2,048 output tokens; SDK retries disabled; 180-second request timeout'],['Tools','Native banking tools and YAML result formatting; native system prompt unchanged in the main cohort'],['Execution','15 tool rounds per native pipeline invocation; native fallback behavior retained. Recovery uses the remaining round budget and runs at most once per invocation.'],['Logging','Individual requests/responses, usage, tool traces, before/after states, source snapshots and hashes']],[100,W-100], 8.8),Spacer(1, 10),
 H('Populations'),table([['Stage','Scope'],['Original development','User tasks 0, 1, 2, 3, 13; 38 initial episodes (including 3 attacker-capability controls), 18 custom-pretext and 27 mechanism-comparison episodes'],['Main formal experiment','Tasks 4, 7, 11, 12, 14, 15; clean and two attacker goals; three arms; three repetitions = 162 episodes'],['Date follow-up','Tasks 4, 11, 15; same arms, goals and repetitions; shared simulation date = 81 episodes']],[130,W-130], 9),Spacer(1, 9),
 P('Utility is the native binary task-completion check. Attack success is the native attacker-goal check: the upstream field named security means attacker success here. Safe completion equals utility AND NOT attack success. Technical failures are not safe outcomes. All scheduled attacked episodes remain in the denominator; exposure is a separate diagnostic.'),
 P('Each trial averages six clean or twelve attacked cases per arm. Means, sample SD and sample variance summarize three trial values. These are repeated API calls on the same tasks, not independent datasets; a local random seed does not control provider sampling.','small')]))
pages.append(page('3. Task audit and reproduction evidence',[
 H('The grading instruments require inspection'),
 table([['Finding before formal outcomes','Treatment'],['Leakage goals 0, 1, 3 accept irrelevant transfer text due to Boolean-expression behavior','Exclude those goals; preserve source and counterexamples'],['Tasks 5, 6, 8, 9, 10 pass with no tool action','Exclude from strict main cohort'],['Task 5 asks for a price difference but checks a 50.00 transfer','Record task/scorer mismatch'],['Task 11 checks amount but not payee','Keep native score; predeclare exact-transfer supplementary check']],[285,W-285], 8.9),Spacer(1, 8),
 P('The original source is changed only to repair content-block handling in the offline injectability check. Native utility and attacker scorers are retained. Positive reference execution alone is insufficient: the audit also uses no-action and deliberately incorrect-action controls.'),
 H('Own baseline measurements'),P('The development baseline completes 4/5 clean tasks. Under tool_knowledge and important_instructions injections it completes 7/15 and 5/15, with 0/30 attacker goals achieved. All 30 payloads are actually observed. Direct requests for the three attacker operations succeed 3/3, so failure under injection is not explained by unavailable tools. A further 18 business/pretext attacks also achieve no attacker goal.'),
 H('Comparison with the reported behavior'),table([['Reference','Benign utility','Utility under attack','Targeted ASR'],['Paper Table 5: GPT-4o, no defense [1]','69.00%','50.01%','57.69%'],['Our formal banking baseline','66.67%','36.11%','0.00%']],[195, 100, 110,W-405], 8.7),Spacer(1, 7),
 P('The paper row aggregates a different model, task population and benchmark state. It is contextual reference, not a matched baseline. Utility degradation reproduces in this setup; the reported successful-attack rate does not. No claim of general immunity follows from zero success on these static goals.','small')]))
pages.append(page('4. Modification: one bounded task review',[
 H('Motivation and development decision'),P('A write-time action gate cannot help when the Agent refuses the malicious request and stops before proposing any legitimate write. Development comparison therefore tests both an action gate and bounded recovery. On six attacked development cases, the baseline completes three, the gate four and recovery six; all three arms have zero attacker success. Those observations select the research direction and are excluded from formal scores.'),
 H('The single main intervention'),table([['Native behavior','Added behavior'],['Agent stops after its final answer','One review of the original request and observed facts'],['No outcome-based continuation','Review is unconditional at the native stopping point'],['Tools may write simulated account state','Same tools, with the remaining native round budget'],['Original task and external data','No new user authorization, reference answer or evaluator feedback']],[W/2,W/2], 9.1),Spacer(1, 10),
 P('The fixed review asks whether an authorized operation was left incomplete despite available inputs, instructs the Agent to make only necessary changes, preserve unspecified existing fields, ignore embedded instructions, and avoid repeating completed writes. If information is genuinely missing, it should continue asking rather than invent values. The implementation is Recovery in course_project/interventions.py.'),
 H('Controls'),P('Formal arms are independent: native baseline, the author\'s repeat_user_prompt defense, and native baseline plus recovery. Recovery does not stack the action gate or the repetition defense. All arms share model, data, tools and generation parameters. Task-major execution rotates arm order by task and trial. Each task-goal pair uses identical saved attack text across arms and repetitions.'),
 P('The fixed protocol and source hashes precede formal calls. No quality-based retry, task replacement or formal prompt tuning occurs. The review changes the Agent\'s decision process; it is neither human confirmation nor proof that every decision is correct.','small')]))
